{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"deliver","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"destinations","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Destination","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Destinations11DestinationP"},{"text":"..., ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchBufferLimit","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":" = 100) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsynchronousUnitOfWork","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent22AsynchronousUnitOfWorkP"},{"text":"<()>\n","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Where each batch goes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"destinations"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"How many batches each destination may have waiting while it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"still receiving an earlier one."}]}],"name":"batchBufferLimit"}]},{"content":[{"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A unit of work that completes once the last batch is delivered, and throws what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the sequence throws, or "},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when cancelled."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"code":["let delivery = tracker.records","    .batch(strategy: .count(20))","    .deliver(to: ConsoleDestination(), vendor)","try await delivery.execute()"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each destination receives its batches in order, one at a time, from a buffer of its own,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so a slow destination delays only itself. When a batch arrives while a destination’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"buffer already holds ","type":"text"},{"code":"batchBufferLimit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" batches, the oldest waiting batch is dropped.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Once the sequence ends, the work completes after every destination has received its last","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Records a store keeps (those with an ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord.deliveryTag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") are reported to it:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before a batch goes to any destination, and again once every destination’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"receive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has returned for it without being cancelled, when the store may forget them. A record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the store couldn’t mark as being delivered is left out of the batch, and a batch left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with no records isn’t sent.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Records the delivery has read but not delivered are lost to this run when it is cancelled"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or fails, and so are batches a destination’s full buffer dropped. Without a store they are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gone; a store never had them acknowledged, so it delivers them on the next launch (unless"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its bound drops them first, which it reports)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing runs until the work is executed, and each execution reads the sequence again, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a delivery that finished or failed can be executed again (a retry). Cancelling it drops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the batches its destinations had waiting, and is permanent, as for every Afluent unit of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"work: executing a cancelled delivery again throws "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CancellationError"},{"type":"text","text":" at once, so build a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"new one instead."}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"batchBufferLimit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is at least 1.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Precondition"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/destinations\/_concurrency\/asyncsequence\/deliver(to:batchbufferlimit:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Deliver.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Destinations\/Deliver.swift#L46"},"modules":[{"name":"Destinations","relatedModules":["_Concurrency"]}],"conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Element"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[EventRecord]"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"title":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:)","extendedModule":"_Concurrency","roleHeading":"Instance Method","externalID":"s:Sci12Destinationss8SendableRzSay6Events1